# a single `mode=raid` pull against The Long Cold, never a full evening.
# And every `dodge`-style evening on record so far was a tank (paladin:
# protection, 2026-09-26-19, 25-heroic) -- this is the first `dodge`
# evening on a pure melee-dps role, the first at 10-normal, and the first
# on a genuinely fresh save with a desktop (non-touch) viewport. `dodge`
# never calls an ability at all (scripts/playbot.ts), so on a melee spec
# with no ranged option this is as strict a test of #1's "doing nothing
# wins" as idle's own melee reading (2026-09-27-10, druid:feral) -- except
# `dodge` actively steers away from danger the whole time, where idle never
# moves, so this also asks whether that steering changes how THE VIGIL
# corridor plays out (#6) or whether a travel-mode wipe under a moving,
# never-attacking body still stalls PULL AGAIN the way #271 has under
# every style tried there so far.
